Chapter-walking agentic review of the morloc documentation.

A single user-chosen persona walks src/index.adoc one included .asc file at
a time, in order. For each chapter, an agent runs every code example on a
VM (completing partial code where needed), cross-checks the morloc compiler
when in doubt, and writes two files:

  findings/reports/<chapter>.md      — issues found in this chapter
  findings/summaries/<chapter>.md    — 100-line knowledge snapshot for the
                                       next chapter agent

Every subsequent chapter agent gets all prior summaries folded into its
context, so morloc knowledge accumulates without re-feeding raw docs. Every
chapter agent also receives the same user-supplied focus.

An optional final analyst step consolidates every report into
findings/action-plan.md.

Prerequisites
-------------
  - vagrant + vagrant-libvirt plugin
  - claude CLI (Claude Code)
  - A local morloc-manager binary (or symlink to one) placed next to the
    Vagrantfile. The VM provisioner installs from /vagrant/morloc-manager
    and will refuse to boot if it is missing. Typical setup:

      cd chapter-agents/
      ln -s ../../../compiler/morloc/out/morloc-manager morloc-manager

    The synced_folder is configured with --copy-links, so a symlink to the
    compiled binary is fine.

Quick start
-----------
  ./test/run-chapters.sh --info                          # list personas + chapters
  ./test/run-chapters.sh -p skeptical-tester             # full run
  ./test/run-chapters.sh -p spec-lawyer \
      --chapters getting-started,features-functions \
      --no-destroy                                       # 2-chapter dry run
  ./test/run-chapters.sh -p curious-newbie \
      --start-at features-effects --no-setup             # resume mid-run

Adding a persona
----------------
Drop a markdown file into test/personas/. First line is a one-sentence
descriptor (shown by --info). See existing personas for the pattern.

Layout
------
  Vagrantfile                     Fedora + Docker + morloc-manager (same as doc-agents)
  test/run-chapters.sh            orchestrator
  test/chapter-context.md         common instructions injected into every agent
  test/analyst-context.md         instructions for the final consolidator
  test/personas/*.md              persona definitions
  findings/reports/*.md           per-chapter issue reports (created on first run)
  findings/summaries/*.md         per-chapter knowledge snapshots
  findings/action-plan.md         consolidated output

Compared to the neighboring pipelines
-------------------------------------
  doc-agents/       parallel code-tester + reviewers, multi-pass, all-docs-at-once
  coding-agents/    persona rotation, one project per run, docs-bundle-based
  chapter-agents/   one persona, chapter-by-chapter, summaries chain forward
